Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 14:53:45 +0200
Subject: Backport the io.virtualDirectory factory from the 3.10 stream

The 3.10 stream's "Improve IO package encapsulation" (upstream da99eb87b0)
made the VirtualDirectory constructor private[io] and introduced a package-
level factory as the sanctioned way to obtain an in-memory directory.
Backporting the factory lets tools that drive the compiler (Soundness's
anthology) compile against the same API on both streams, instead of relying
on the constructor where it happens to be public.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude).

Proscala-Patch: virtualdir
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/io/package.scala | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/io/package.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/io/package.scala
index 19bb6e4ad19bee84781dd9d20b10c00e7c96e5de..8d7f054b152f9a8fb12b3f38da848caeabf88e87 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/io/package.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/io/package.scala
@@ -9,4 +9,12 @@ package object io {
   type JManifest = java.util.jar.Manifest
   type JFile = java.io.File
   type JPath = java.nio.file.Path
+
+  // Backported from the 3.10 stream ("Improve IO package encapsulation",
+  // upstream da99eb87b0), where the VirtualDirectory constructor became
+  // private[io] and this factory is the sanctioned way to obtain an in-memory
+  // directory. Providing it here lets tooling compile against the same API on
+  // both streams.
+  def virtualDirectory(name: String): AbstractFile =
+    new VirtualDirectory(name)
 }
